<title>USA: U.S. Office names vice-chairman, COO.</title>
<headline>U.S. Office names vice-chairman, COO.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Office Products Co said Tuesday that Timothy Flynn had been named vice chairman and Tom Morgan had been named chief operating officer.</p>
<p>&quot;Flynn will now focus on directing the effort to realize important operating synergies from USOP's recently announced acquisition of Mail Boxes Etc,&quot; the company said in a statement. The acquisition is awaiting regulatory and shareholder approval and is expected to close in August.</p>
<p>Flynn formerly served as president and COO. Morgan previously served as president of the company's North American Office Products Group.</p>
</text>
